  {section %title=Introduction
    {references %title=Reference %id=R
{ref %id=SMP %edition=Rev.1 (5 August 2025) %ref=ECSS-E-ST-40-07C %href=https://ecss.nl/standard/ecss-e-st-40-07c-rev-1-simulation-modelling-platform-level-1-5-august-2025/ %%Simulation Modelling Platform (SMP) Level 1}
{ref %id=SMPL2 %edition=5 August 2025 %ref=ECSS-E-ST-40-08C %href=https://ecss.nl/standard/ecss-e-st-40-08c-simulation-modelling-platform-level-2-5-august-2025/ %%Simulation Modelling Platform (SMP) Level 2}
    }
    {section %title=Scope
The simdeck component is a library of C++ classes implementing the SMP {xref SMP}
interfaces needed for models and optional services development. This is
part of the simphonie project and is used for the simphonie own implementation
of a SMP simulation infrastructure. Simdeck may be used with our without
simphonie. It is expected to deliver with simdeck a compliant implementation of
the SMP interfaces in order to let any model or service built on top of simdeck
run into any SMP compliant simulation infrastructure.

This definition file includes:
  - traceability requirement: identification of the implemented SMP interfaces.
  - few design considerations.
  - a test plan.
  - a user's guide, the targeted user being a model or optional service
    developer that wish to deliver simulation artefact able to be hosted by
    a SMP simulation infrastructure.
    }
  }
  {section %title=Requirements
    {section %title=Requirements definition
The requirements in this document are defined and rendered using the following
layout:
{reqsample %id=req.unique.identifier
A sentence applying the format <subject> shall <property> defining a verifiable  characteristic of the subject.

{rational
Optional information providing some motivation and justification of the
requirement.
}
}
Any text outside the requirement box is only additional information for a better
understanding of the requirement and its scope. Such text shall net define any
property to be verified. When such text is inserted between requirement, without
any reference, is related to the preceding requirement.
    }
    {section %title=Some SMP Level 1 concrete classes
{req %id=simdeck.1
The simphonie project shall include a SMP development kit aming at providing the
concrete classes of the SMP interfaces needed to develop some components
(services and models) libraries.

{rational
The SMP headers only defines pure virtual C++ classes requiring the simulator
and models implementers to define every methods implementation. Many interfaces
are designed to be used on both model and infrastructure side. Having the
related concrete classes available speed-up the models and infrastructure
development.   
}
}
The SMP development kit library is expected to provide what's needed for users
models and services development. It is not expected to provide any
implementation for the infrastructure side components (for instance the
simulator and its mandatory services implementation). Such simulation host
implementation is left to the simphonie project. Even simdeck is part of the
simphonie project, it may be used for any SMP component development outside
simphonie.

{req %id=simdeck.2
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IObject}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.3
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IComponent}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.4
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IComposite}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.5
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::ICollection}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.6
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IContainer}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.7
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IEntryPoint}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.8.1
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IEntryPointPublisher}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.8.2
The entry point publisher implementation shall provide a method to create an
entry point directly from a void class method without argument.

{rational
Let the model or service implementer directly promote any of the component's method as an entry point that may be scheduled or subscribed to the event manager.
}
}

{req %id=simdeck.9
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IException}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.1
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete classe for the {kw Smp::IField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.2
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete classe for the {kw Smp::IPersist}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.3
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IOutputField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.4
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::ISimpleField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.5
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class implementing both 
{kw Smp::ISimpleField} and {kw Smp::IOutputField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.6
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IArrayField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.7
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::ISimpleArrayField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.8
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class implementing both 
{kw Smp::ISimpleArrayField} and {kw Smp::IOutputField}
interface.
}

{req %id=simdeck.10.9
The SMP development kit shall provide a concrete class for the {kw Smp::IStructureField}
