    {section %title=Additional utility classes
      {section %title=Variable length string field
{req %id=simdeck.addon.str.1
The simdeck library shall provide a {kw Smp::Publication::IType} implementation
of non fixed sized string fields.

{rational
Let models and services implementers manage string parameters without the
constraint of oversized fixed memory allocation.
}
}

{req %id=simdeck.addon.str.2
The simdeck library shall provide a {kw Smp::IField} implementation to wrap a
C++ {kw std::string} parameter.

{rational
std::string type is now th emost common way of handling strings with C++.
}
}

{req %id=simdeck.addon.str.3
The simdeck library shall provide a {kw Smp::IField} implementation to wrap a
C++ {kw std::string} parameter.

{rational
std::string type is now the most common way of handling strings with C++.
}
}
      }
      {section %title=Zero copy fields
{req %id=simdeck.zcf.1
The simdeck library shall provide a {kw Smp::IOutputField} implementation able
to share its data with connected fields.

{rational
The SMP publication mecanisme and field handling was designed to make the model
implementation quite agnostic from the simulation infrastructure, requiring the
model to only share some pointers to its data. A more optimized memory
management would required the model to request its memory from the simulation
infrastructure to let when relevant, the infrastructure provide the same buffer
pointer to be shared between a data producer and its consumers. A dedicated
field type may provide the same capability.

Such buffer sharing can brings high performance increase: in many cases, the
simulator spent more time to copy data from outputs to inputs than to compute
anything.
}
}
The zero copy field type is compatible with itself only: it is admitted it can
work only when both producer and consumer of a data are managing it using the
same field class family that extends consistently the {kw SMp::IField}
interface to do so. Such field are necessary automatic fields, meaning the
output data is pushed every time it is changed since the push finally does
nothing because the same buffer is shared between the connected fields.

As well, sharing the same buffer implies the users (simulators designers) are
aware such fields shall be used (read and written) sequentially only, meaning
from entry points executed from the same thread.

{req %id=simdeck.zcf.2
The simdeck library zero copy fields feature shall cover all the SMP primitive
types.
}

{req %id=simdeck.zcf.3
The simdeck library zero copy fields feature shall define the cast operators to
let the fields type assignable to their related primitive type and the opposite.

{rational
The model implementer shall be able to use the field the same way it would use
the wrapped data. It shall not require to use explicit setter or getters to 
access the value. The code using the fields will then remain as readable than
the equivalent code using the native unboxed data.
}
}
      }
      {section %title=Bus fields
The purpose of the feature is to be able to create many to one and many to many
fields connections.
- define something similar to matlab/simulinks bus features.
- shall it be derive from Smp::IField (connectable by itself) or IComponent
conectable with the ILink registrey.
- quite obvious to push many outputs into a single thing. But how to select
cells when connecting inputs?

      }
    }
  }
  {section %title=Design
    {section %title=Zero copy fields
Zero copy fields aree implemented the same way the "standard" fields are. The
differences are:
  - it manages a buffer and a pointer. The pointer defines the data wrapped by
    the field. When not connected, the pointer is the address of the internal
    buffer. When connected, the pointer is the address of the connected field's
    internal buffer.
  - on connect, the output field push its buffer address to the target field.
  - on disconnect, the target field shall be notify to restore its data pointer
    to its own buffer address.

Of course, the buffer pointer sharing is applied only when both source and
destination are zero copy fields. Otherwise the regular data propagation process
shall be applied.
    }
  }
  {section %title=Validation plan
    {section %title=Strategy
The simdeck classes shall be fully covered by unit tests. The test are
implemented with the help of the cppunit library and additional helper macro
from the {a %href=https://gitub.com/seeduvax/AcrobatomicBuildSystem %%AcrobatomaticBuildSystem},
to support requirement traceability management. The next section provide the
unit test index.
    }
